{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Ce4mTdnLPFcdTrevN6oHw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I would add the new rule to section 2, immediately after the existing timeout bullet, as follows:\n\n```markdown\n## 2. Failure handling\n\n- **Retries are bounded and jittered.** Every retry wrapper declares\n  its maximum attempt count at the call site; backoff is exponential\n  with jitter, and a non-retriable error class aborts immediately —\n  enumerate those classes beside the wrapper, not in a distant\n  constants file.\n- **Timeouts are explicit.** No call inherits a library default\n  timeout silently; the call site states its per-attempt timeout.\n- **Wall-clock caps prevent indefinite retrying.** A per-attempt timeout\n  with unbounded attempts still hangs the caller; declare both the\n  attempt cap and the wall-clock cap at the call site.\n\n## 3. Recording outcomes\n```\n\n**Placement rationale:** This rule is a critical refinement of the timeout and retry policies already established in section 2. It directly addresses the interaction between the two existing bullets and prevents a dangerous loophole where complying with both rules independently could still cause hangs—making it essential context for anyone implementing the earlier requirements."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":411,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":264,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}}
